Newspeak3
'Test'
(* newspeak-spec.pdf 6.1: an inheritance clause that does not appear within
   an enclosing class "is evaluated as if it was a top level expression" --
   a top level expression (3.8) has no enclosing object to send to. So a
   module's root class may inherit only Object or Value, or write
   Object <: Value, and its superclass clause may send only `new`, the one
   factory both answer; `Object foo` is a defect (`docs/design/object-model.md`,
   "The root rule").

   The rule is checked by the resolver, before anything runs: a module
   whose artifact `build` could never write must not run under `run`
   either, so this is a resolve error and `main:args:` never runs
   (`docs/design/README.md`, "Deviations from the language specification"). *)
class RootSendsOtherThanNew = Object foo () (
    public main: platform args: arguments = (
        platform transcript show: 'unreachable'; newLine
    )
) : ()
